A few days back Anthropic's Applied AI team wrote ["Effective context engineering for AI agents"](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents). This is something that I've been feeling but haven't yet put into words: getting the AI into the right "frame of mind" by supplying context and correct follow-on prompts is at least as important as the right seed prompt.

It lines up with recent themes on my blog: that effective AI work is management and context design, not wordsmithing ([The power of the pause](/posts/20250923-effective-ai-work-is-project-management/)); that integration beats bolt‑ons ([Smart AI integration comes only with knowledge](/posts/20250919-smart-ai-integration-context-first/)); and that technical writers are becoming "context curators" so agents can truly RTFM ([AI must RTFM](/posts/20250929-ai-must-rtfm-context-curators/)).

{% endmarkdown %}


